{#
/**
 * @file
 * The Preserve usage explorer. Bootstrap 5 markup themed with Lehigh brand
 * tokens in css/explorer.css; js/explorer.js binds to the data-* attributes.
 */
#}
<div class="lu-explorer" data-lehigh-explorer data-bs-theme="light">
  <nav class="lu-nav d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center border-bottom" aria-label="Usage explorer sections">
    <ul class="nav me-auto">
      <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="#lu-overview">Overview</a></li>
      <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="#lu-distribution">Distribution</a></li>
      <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="#lu-documents">Documents</a></li>
      <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="#lu-methods">About the data</a></li>
    </ul>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-copy>Copy link</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-theme aria-pressed="false">Dark mode</button>
  </nav>

  <header class="lu-masthead" id="lu-overview">
    <p class="lu-eyebrow">Lehigh University · The Preserve</p>
    <h1>Usage <span>Explorer</span></h1>
    <p class="lu-intro lead">Explore how The Preserve’s collections are read and downloaded. Discover the works reaching readers at Lehigh and around the world.</p>
    <p class="lu-meta small text-body-secondary mb-0" data-updated>Repository usage · Page views and downloads reported separately</p>
  </header>

  <form class="lu-filters card card-body" data-filters>
    <div class="lu-filter-grid">
      <div class="lu-period">
        <label class="form-label" for="lu-period">Reporting period</label>
        <select class="form-select" id="lu-period" name="period">{% for key, period in periods %}<option value="{{ key }}">{{ period.label }}</option>{% endfor %}</select>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label class="form-label" for="lu-field">Filter by metadata</label>
        <select class="form-select" id="lu-field" data-field>{% for name, label in fields %}<option value="{{ name }}"{% if name == 'field_model' %} selected{% endif %}>{{ label }}</option>{% endfor %}</select>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label class="form-label" for="lu-search">Matching values</label>
        <input class="form-control" id="lu-search" type="search" placeholder="Type to search and add values…" maxlength="100" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="lu-filter-help lu-options-status" data-search>
      </div>
      <div class="lu-filter-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary" data-more-options hidden>Show more matches</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-reset>Reset</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="lu-hint mt-2 mb-0" id="lu-filter-help">Select one or more values. Values in the same field match any; different fields match together. Only choices with matching usage are offered.</p>
    <p class="lu-hint mb-0" id="lu-options-status" data-options-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary mt-2" data-retry-filters hidden>Retry filters</button>
    <div class="lu-chips d-flex flex-wrap gap-2" data-chips aria-label="Active metadata filters"></div>
  </form>

  <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2 my-3">
    <p class="lu-status small text-body-secondary mb-0" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading saved usage totals…</p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-retry hidden>Retry reports</button>
  </div>
  <noscript><p>This explorer needs JavaScript for interactive filtering. <a href="{{ path('lehigh_analytics.public_export', {report: 'types'}) }}">Download usage by content type as CSV</a>.</p></noscript>

  <div data-results hidden>
    <section class="lu-kpis card mb-4" aria-label="Usage totals">
      <div class="row row-cols-2 row-cols-lg-4 g-0">
        <div class="col"><span>Page views</span><strong data-kpi="views">—</strong><small>Visits to repository records</small></div>
        <div class="col"><span>Downloads</span><strong data-kpi="downloads">—</strong><small>Recorded media requests</small></div>
        <div class="col"><span>Countries &amp; Territories</span><strong data-kpi="countries">—</strong><small>Excludes unknown locations</small></div>
        <div class="col"><span>Collections used</span><strong data-kpi="collections">—</strong><small>Direct collection membership</small></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="row g-4" id="lu-distribution" aria-label="Usage distribution">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
        <article class="card h-100"><div class="card-body">
          <div class="lu-panel-heading"><div><p class="lu-eyebrow">Content type</p><h2>Usage by Islandora Model</h2></div><a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-export="types">CSV ↓</a></div>
          <p class="lu-hint">Select a model to explore its usage.</p>
          <div class="lu-legend"><span>Page views</span><span>Downloads</span></div>
          <div data-chart="types"></div>
        </div></article>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
        <article class="card h-100"><div class="card-body">
          <div class="lu-panel-heading"><div><p class="lu-eyebrow">Collections</p><h2>Where readers explore</h2></div><a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-export="collections">CSV ↓</a></div>
          <p class="lu-hint">Top 10 by page views. Select a collection to filter.</p>
          <div class="lu-legend"><span>Page views</span><span>Downloads</span></div>
          <div data-chart="collections"></div>
        </div></article>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
        <article class="card h-100 lu-countries"><div class="card-body">
          <div class="lu-panel-heading"><div><p class="lu-eyebrow">Global reach</p><h2>Usage around the world</h2></div><a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-export="countries">CSV ↓</a></div>
          <div class="lu-table-scroll table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-hover align-middle mb-0">
              <thead><tr><th scope="col">Country / Territory</th><th scope="col" class="text-end">Page views</th><th scope="col" class="text-end">Downloads</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody data-countries></tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p class="lu-hint" data-geo-note></p>
        </div></article>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
        <article class="card h-100 lu-notes"><div class="card-body">
          <p class="lu-eyebrow">Reading the numbers</p>
          <h2>Every view tells part of the story.</h2>
          <p>Page views count visits to a work’s record. Downloads count requests for associated media. They are distinct measures, not unique readers.</p>
          <p>A work may belong to more than one model or collection, so grouped totals may overlap.</p>
          <p>Country and territory coverage depends on location data recorded with each event. “Unknown location” is shown separately and excluded from the distinct count.</p>
          <a href="#lu-methods">See definitions and reporting notes ↗</a>
        </div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card mt-4 lu-documents" id="lu-documents"><div class="card-body">
      <div class="lu-panel-heading"><div><p class="lu-eyebrow">Most used works</p><h2>Top 100 documents</h2></div><a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-export="views" data-works-export>Download CSV ↓</a></div>
      <div class="lu-table-tools">
        <div class="btn-group" role="group" aria-label="Document ranking">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary active" data-rank="views" aria-pressed="true">By page views</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary" data-rank="downloads" aria-pressed="false">By downloads</button>
        </div>
        <label class="lu-work-search">Search these results <input class="form-control" type="search" data-work-search placeholder="Document title…"></label>
        <span class="lu-work-count" data-work-count></span>
      </div>
      <div class="lu-table-scroll table-responsive">
        <table class="table table-hover align-middle mb-0">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Rank</th><th scope="col">Document</th><th scope="col" class="text-end">Page views</th><th scope="col" class="text-end">Downloads</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody data-works></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div></section>
  </div>

  <details class="lu-methods card card-body mt-4" id="lu-methods">
    <summary>About the data &amp; reporting downloads</summary>
    <p>Source: Entity Metrics joined to current Islandora metadata. Only published works available to anonymous readers are included. Staff-cookie events are excluded. These are recorded events, not COUNTER-certified counts, unique readers, or verified human activity.</p>
    <p>Calendar years begin January 1; fiscal years begin July 1. “Latest completed” excludes the current year. All time means all recorded history, which may not cover the repository’s entire lifetime. Totals refresh in the background; the update time is shown above.</p>
    <p>Top-document rankings exclude Collection and component Page models. Collection reports use direct membership. Filters combine with AND across fields and OR within a field.</p>
    <p data-coverage></p>
    <p>These worksheets help prepare standards reports; definitions, exclusions, and the reporting year must be reviewed before submission.</p>
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-export="counter">COUNTER mapping worksheet ↓</a>
      <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-export="acrl">ACRL preparation worksheet ↓</a>
      <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-export="top_types_views">Top 100 per model · page views ↓</a>
      <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-export="top_types_downloads">Top 100 per model · downloads ↓</a>
    </div>
  </details>
</div>
